          deckDescription: 'A 32-card stripped deck: four French suits with ranks 7 through Ace (Ace high). Pilotta is a trick-taking game; the full pack is dealt and a turned card or bid sets trump; players take tricks and score points.',
          suitDescription: 'The four French suits (hearts, diamonds, clubs, spades) each have eight cards in the 32-card deck. In Pilotta, following suit is required when able; trump beats plain suits; suit and rank determine trick winners.',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks 7, 8, 9, 10, Jack, Queen, King, Ace in each suit; Ace is high. Trick order is standard: highest card of the led suit wins unless trumped; within trump the same order applies.',
